<title>USA: Honeywell gets Measurex clearance.</title>
<headline>Honeywell gets Measurex clearance.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honeywell Inc said Friday it received early antitrust clearance under the Hart-Scott-Rodino Act for its proposed acquisition of Measurex Corp.</p>
<p>Clearance was granted by the U.S. Department of Justice and the Federal Trade Commission.  </p>
<p>Under terms of the previously announced merger between Honeywell and Measurex, a wholly owned subsidiary of Honeywell began a tender offer on January 27 for all outstanding Measurex shares at $35 per share.</p>
<p>That offer will expire at midnight February 28, unless extended.</p>
<p>Honeywell is a controls manufacturer.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
